-## 10. Edge Functions
+## A6) “Public Profile Shape” (Discovery/Profile Preview) — REQUIRED
+
+Because `profiles` is private, implement one of these two patterns:
+
+### Pattern A (Preferred): RPC returns whitelisted fields
+RPC returns only safe fields (no legal_name, phone, precise coordinates, raw dob).
+Example safe shape: id, display_name, social_id, verification_status, tier, district_name, pet_species_summary, avatar_url (signed), etc.
+
+### Pattern B: `profiles_public_view`
+If you choose a view, it must reference only safe fields and still enforce exclusions (non_social, blocks) at query layer (RPC/Edge) if needed.
+
+**Hard rule:** clients must never do `select * from profiles where id=...` for other users.
 
-**`create-marketplace-booking`:**
-- Creates Stripe PaymentIntent
-- Inserts `marketplace_bookings` row
-- Returns Stripe Checkout URL
+---
 
-**`check-and-increment-quota`:**
-- Security definer function
-- Checks quota before action
-- Increments counter if allowed
-- Returns boolean
+## A7) Required SECURITY DEFINER RPCs (Signatures + Contracts)
 
-**`process-dispute-resolution`:**
-- Admin-only
-- Executes Stripe Transfer or Refund
-- Updates booking status
+> Names can vary, but these behaviors must exist.
 
-**`stripe-webhook`:**
-- Listens for `payment_intent.succeeded`
-- Updates `marketplace_bookings` status
-- Verifies webhook signature
+### A7.1 Social ID availability
+```sql
+create or replace function public.is_social_id_taken(candidate text)
+returns boolean
+language sql
+security definer
+as $$
+  select exists (
+    select 1 from public.profiles
+    where lower(social_id) = lower(candidate)
+  );
+$$;
+```
+
+### A7.2 QMS snapshot (UI-safe)
+- Must return remaining counts where allowed (AI uploads remaining, stars remaining, broadcasts remaining)
+- Must NOT return cap totals for hidden-caps features.
+
+### A7.3 check_and_increment_quota(action_type)
+- Locks `user_quotas` row FOR UPDATE
+- Applies rolling window reset logic
+- Increments only on success
+
+### A7.4 create_broadcast_alert(...)
+Must be atomic and in this order:
+1) lock quotas
+2) derive tier (server)
+3) enforce active slot cap (10) using `map_alerts` where expires_at > now()
+4) enforce monthly quota / super credits
+5) insert
+6) decrement
+7) return id + remaining (no cap totals)
+
+### A7.5 send_star_open_conversation(target_user_id)
+- Deducts star ONLY if conversation successfully created/opened
+- Atomic (lock quotas row + create room + deduct)
+
+### A7.6 get_discovery_stack(filters json)
+- Enforces tier gating of filters server-side
+- Applies non_social exclusion + block exclusion bidirectional
+- Applies skip TTL table
+- Returns safe profile shape only
 
